{"base_rate":0.36723910171730517,"brier":0.13853513870541612,"bss":0.40382824905002934,"bss_hi":0.4808184264537414,"bss_lo":0.3071555736241838,"chart":{"base":[379.5,134.5],"fp":[293.1,216.7],"lead":"62,211.8 272,205.6 482,187.3 692,145.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.40 — higher than 75% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +16pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 16% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 6%; promised 100% → rained 86%"},"rel":"68.7,438.7 232.9,358.7 552.2,213.5 690.3,95.7"},"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09163804491413477,"ess":410.43585752273975,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Malmoe</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Malmoe rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>86%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMALMO A, 5.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.40, ranked 53 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(26&ndash;100) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>161</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Malmoe</b> <span class=\"muted\">Sweden</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;37% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 37% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.40</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>26&ndash;100\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Malmoe &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Malmoe\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.07831858407079,380.3893805309734 72.868,348.02666666666664 117.90415584415585,287.4545454545455 190.65684210526317,204.78947368421052 296.75864864864866,101.62162162162161 373.4244117647059,34.05882352941177 411.03254658385094,18.0 411.03254658385094,22.52173913043481 373.4244117647059,82.23529411764707 296.75864864864866,175.40540540540542 190.65684210526317,281.42105263157896 117.90415584415585,348.9090909090909 72.868,382.0 58.07831858407079,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"248.32496697490092\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"248.32496697490092\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.07831858407079,370.72566371681415 72.868,323.76 117.90415584415585,320.54545454545456 190.65684210526317,262.2631578947368 296.75864864864866,200.0 373.4244117647059,135.76470588235293 411.03254658385094,70.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 226 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.07831858407079\" cy=\"370.72566371681415\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"72.868\" cy=\"323.76\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 17%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"117.90415584415585\" cy=\"320.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 37%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"190.65684210526317\" cy=\"262.2631578947368\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"296.75864864864866\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 68% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"373.4244117647059\" cy=\"135.76470588235293\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 161 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.03254658385094\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(37%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Malmoe the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.49) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.32).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>0.316</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.332</td><td class='num'>9.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.390</td><td class='num'>8.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.487</td><td class='num'>10.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":55.60587,"lon":13.00073,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Malmoe","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00022123893805309737,"n":226,"obs":0.030973451327433628,"sig":true},{"hi":0.09,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.042,"n":75,"obs":0.16,"sig":true},{"hi":0.27,"lo":0.09,"mean":0.16922077922077924,"n":77,"obs":0.16883116883116883,"sig":false},{"hi":0.5160000000000008,"lo":0.27,"mean":0.37473684210526315,"n":76,"obs":0.32894736842105265,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.5160000000000008,"mean":0.6744594594594595,"n":74,"obs":0.5,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.891029411764706,"n":68,"obs":0.6764705882352942,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9972670807453416,"n":161,"obs":0.8571428571428571,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.9,"provisional":false,"rank":53,"rank_hi":100.07499999999993,"rank_lo":26.0,"reliability":0.013158882792901888,"resolution":0.10352205367470346,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"malmoe","station":"MALMO A","timezone":"Europe/Stockholm"}